WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.560
~Monday~

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.840
Oh, what shall we do?

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.080
This is terrible.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.110
I can't believe it. We'd forgotten
something really important.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.150
I wonder what could be the matter.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.520
No idea.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.650
Rei-chan, did you guys forget something?

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.760
The farewell event for the Lady Roses...

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.370
What? But we have prepared for it right here...

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.010
No, that's preparation for the
send-off of the graduates...

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.570
...that we're doing as the student council.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.010
It's separate from the farewell
event for the Lady Roses...

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.140
...that we do as boutons.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.810
I had no idea there was such an event, too.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.160
We were so busy and distracted,

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.450
we overlooked this important matter.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:06.390
Indeed. This is an error most
unbecoming of us boutons.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.730
Well, it's good that we noticed it in advance,

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.930
but we need to get in touch with the
Lady Roses as soon as possible.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.400
Um, if that's the case, I can do that.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.140
Oh, really? That will be a great help, Yumi-chan.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.230
Then I will go right away.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.330
Yumi, wait.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.600
We have yet to even decide
when we are doing this.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.110
You are really so lacking in composure.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:34.850
Try not to get too carried away.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.250
R-Right.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.670
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.300
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.240
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.340
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.610
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.910
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:09.420
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.330
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:31.580
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:38.450
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:45.960
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:53.590
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:02:54.270 --> 00:03:01.270
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:08.520
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:16.620
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:24.130
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:31.140
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:39.070
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.920
Most Dreadfully Busy Days

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.410
So, with regards to the farewell event...

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.260
How does Saturday afternoon
sound for you, Rosa Chinensis?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.100
Oh, I hadn't heard anything about it,

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.460
so I was thinking there
might not be one this year.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.640
N-Nothing could be farther from the truth.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.140
Are you sure you guys hadn't forgotten about it?

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.960
P-Please.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.730
Of course.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.280
Yes, we would never.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.910
Oh, the farewell event?

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.780
Yes, how does your schedule look?

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.650
I'll make time for it, of course.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.410
Thank you very much.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.080
But you know, Yumi-chan, you seem
to have your act together more now.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.190
You're going to be a bouton soon, after all.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.130
Yes, thank you.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.590
Oh, the farewell event?

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:32.660
Yes.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.060
So, what are you going to do?

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.000
Do?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:38.360
Your hidden talent.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.940
Hidden talent?!

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.000
It's an annual tradition.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.880
The first-year students perform
for the graduating students.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.180
Oh, please!

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:47.580
No, seriously.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.420
Last year, Rei crushed an
apple with one hand...

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:57.360
...and Sachiko did a solo
song and ballet routine.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.390
I have not heard about any of this.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.630
It's something she swallowed her
pride to do to get some laughs,

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.070
so of course she wouldn't tell her little sister.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.230
She probably doesn't even
want to be reminded of it.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.640
Surely not...

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.280
Well, you're free to believe me or not,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.280
but I'm telling you now, so my darling
Yumi-chan won't be caught in a bind...

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.220
...when she's suddenly asked to perform.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.540
~Tuesday~

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:33.730
Yumi-san, are you sure Rosa
Gigantea isn't pulling your leg?

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.130
Yes, Rei-chan's trick with an apple is one thing,

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:40.900
but to think that Sachiko-sama
would sing and dance on her own...

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.730
But Rosa Gigantea definitely said...

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:47.600
So, she must have been having
a bit of fun at your expense...

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.410
You think so?

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.870
But wait...

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.240
When you really think about it,

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.950
if Sachiko-sama gets provoked, like if
she's told, "I bet you couldn't do it,"

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.890
she's the sort who would
stubbornly prove she could.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:01.180
Now that you mention it...

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.260
Maybe it's like Rosa Gigantea said,

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.490
and both Sachiko-sama and Rei-chan...

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:10.090
...just haven't told us because
they're too embarrassed.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.420
Do you suppose we should have
something prepared, after all?

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.300
But making people laugh is not something I...

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:22.980
Don't worry. We won't be expecting that from you.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:27.110
Instead, I think it would be best for
you to take the arts to the extreme.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.050
The... arts?

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.510
Shimako-san, you're an accredited
master of Japanese dance, right?

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:33.480
Yes...

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:39.220
Then, could you perform an improv
dance to a song that I select?

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:42.660
That would be fine, but... why improv?

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.120
Because that sounds more interesting.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.960
And you and I will be in
charge of making them laugh.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.440
Making them laugh?

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.380
I'll do magic. You do some kind of party trick.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.170
What?

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.040
A party trick?

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.240
I'm at such a loss. A party trick?

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.980
To begin with, I've never
even been to a formal party.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.180
Well, keep looking in there...

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.990
...and you'll find a prop
or two that you can use.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.660
Is it really true that our father's
good at party tricks?

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:21.260
That's the kind of man he is.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.300
I wonder what this is.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.170
Uh, that's...

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:30.670
What's this?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:34.740
A cassette tape, a hand towel,
a 5-yen coin, and a bamboo sieve?

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.820
What's wrong, Yuki?

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.180
I was just reminded of something unpleasant.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:42.550
What?

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.130
I was...

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:49.220
...once forced by my upperclassmen
to use those to perform.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.620
Really...

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.830
So, was it well-received?

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.730
And what if it was?

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.930
Please teach this performance to me!

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.870
You're going to voluntarily turn
yourself into a laughingstock?

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.010
No! I'm going to make them laugh!

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:16.150
~Wednesday~

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:22.560
A one, a two, a three, a four...

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.370
Yumi-san, you seem tired.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.370
Yes, well, the practice has been
more grueling than I expected.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.600
Practice?

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.900
N-Nothing, just something I'm doing...

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.650
A one, a two, a three, a four...

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:41.450
Working hard there, I see.
A one, a two, a three, a four...

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:41.880
Working hard there, I see.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.650
If I'm going to do this,
I'd like the Lady Roses to enjoy it.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.150
~Thursday~

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:59.690
For the Lady Roses... Heave-ho...

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:05.770
Yumi?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.110
Did you carry that all by yourself?

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:09.870
Yes.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:13.080
"Yes"? If you'd let me know, I would've helped.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.080
That's right. Honestly...

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.250
I'm fine. Being energetic is my
only redeeming trait, after all.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.450
I'm off to the flower arrangement club next.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.880
Send-Off
Ceremony
for the
Graduates

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:34.530
Yumi!

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.470
There you go again...

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.600
That thing must weigh at least 10 kilos.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.340
Being energetic is my only redeeming trait, so...

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:49.110
In all seriousness, don't get too carried away.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.080
I'm fine.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:55.560
Because I feel like I'm making
myself useful to my Onee-sama,

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.850
and that makes me happy.

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:09.600
A one, a two, a three, a four...

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:14.100
Hey, why don't you leave it at
that for today and go to sleep?

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.670
Not yet, not yet.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.880
I still don't quite have the
movements of the latter half down.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.740
The performance is the
day after tomorrow, right?

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.580
Why don't you just work on it again tomorrow?

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:23.990
I can't do that!

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.990
Tomorrow is the day before and I'll
be really busy with preparations!

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.550
I have to master it today.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.820
That's fine, but you have
dark circles under your eyes.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.330
What? No way!

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.230
~Friday~

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.200
Yumi-san...

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:59.250
You look rather pale...

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.590
Oh, I didn't quite get enough sleep.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:03.220
Are you all right?

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.750
Yes, physical toughness is the
one area I have confidence in.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.790
Um...

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.540
H-Huh?

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.300
Something's not right...

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:24.740
Yumi-san?!

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:26.580
Yumi-san!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:27.780
Yumi-san?!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.260
Huh?

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.220
Are you awake?

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:40.820
Y-Yes...

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:42.490
Um...

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:44.320
Exhaustion and lack of sleep.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.060
What's going on? It's not even exam season.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.460
Um...

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:50.760
Well, this and that...

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:54.710
You're Ogasawara-san's petite soeur, right?

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:56.140
What? Y-Yes.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.070
She was worried and came by to see you.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.140
What?

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.450
Now that she mentions it...

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:09.020
It'd be best if we could get even a
little something in your stomach.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.220
Do you think you could eat?

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:11.550
Yes...

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:29.300
You dummy.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.000
This is what you get for getting carried away.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.380
On the surface,

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.850
my Onee-sama's words were as cold
as the hand she placed on my brow,

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.690
and yet, somehow, there was a
warmness and melancholy to them...

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.360
This is what I always do.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.390
When I get wrapped up in something,

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.100
I get worked up on my own,

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.930
get carried away all by myself,

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:53.660
and I take things too far and fail.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.770
I'm not worthy of my Onee-sama's kindness.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:08.250
Oh? You're feeling ill enough to cry,
and yet you're eating lunch?

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.410
What's this about?

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:11.980
Rosa Gigantea...

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:15.810
Sensei, I'm here to take charge of Fukuzawa.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:17.690
Can I take her home?

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:20.160
Oh, you're going to accompany her, Sato-san?

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:23.720
Yes. My class is in study hall anyway.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.660
And her mistress asked
me to do her a favor, so...

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:31.500
My Onee-sama did?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.640
Fukuzawa-san?

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:34.980
What do you want to do, Fukuzawa-san?

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.810
I-I am fine now!

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.140
Okay, okay. I get that you're better now.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.480
But you're still going home for today.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:46.320
But there are still preparations for tomorrow...

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.490
Someone else will handle that stuff.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:50.080
That's what friends are for.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:57.420
In fact, they'll be more worried
about you if you're around. Okay?

00:13:58.030 --> 00:13:58.790
All right...

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:07.640
Are you really sure you
want me to leave you here?

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.610
Maybe I should see you all the way home?

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:13.210
No, really... I really am fine now.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:16.210
All right then, Yumi-chan.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.510
Sachiko isn't mad, you know.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.430
Blue
Pit
Viper

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:26.530
Blue
Pit
Viper
Drink this, get your energy back,

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:26.830
Blue
Pit
Viper
and come back tomorrow
with your head held high.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:27.950
and come back tomorrow
with your head held high.

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:32.660
Rosa Gigantea...

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:57.820
Hello?

00:14:58.590 --> 00:14:59.320
Yumi?

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:00.990
Y-Yes!

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:02.790
Are you all right now?

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:07.830
I am so sorry for worrying
and inconveniencing you.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:08.990
No kidding...

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.170
I felt such remorse you know,

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.330
that I had placed too great a burden on you.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:16.110
No, no! It was my fault!

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:20.180
I woke up late, so I ran for the bus
without even eating breakfast.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.220
I hadn't gotten quite enough sleep,

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.240
so I ended up feeling ill. That is all.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:26.980
Not enough sleep?

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:30.050
Yes, because I've been
practicing my hidden talent.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:31.730
Hidden talent?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:35.060
But I will get plenty of sleep tonight...

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.430
...and eat a solid breakfast,

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.400
so I will be at school tomorrow, full of energy.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.900
All right, you do that.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:48.970
My hidden talent...

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.700
I'm still a little worried about it,

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.670
but I have to sleep now,

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:55.770
because it would be bad to worry my Onee-sama.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:03.550
Good morning, Onee-sama.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:07.060
Good morning. Did you have breakfast?

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:08.720
Yes, I did!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.990
If it becomes too much for you, say so.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:13.090
I will!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.230
I'm sorry to have worried you.

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:20.710
It's all good.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:24.210
I mean, for the longest time,
I had my heart ailment to deal with,

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.580
and I wasn't very useful, right?

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.580
So I think I understand how you feel, Yumi-san.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.120
That's right. Don't let it bother you.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.290
I'm used to this sort of
thing with Yoshino anyway.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:37.080
I do not mind filling in at all for someone I like.

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:39.930
Thank you very much.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.830
Now, shall we go to the event hall soon?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.320
Yes!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.250
Oh no, Yumi-san!

